    '<h2 id="what-it-is">What it is</h2>\n' +
    '<p>U01a.B03 separates a framework-free client core from rendering and enforces mechanical import boundaries. It was active at the seeded atlas revision <code>606cba2</code>; fixture-only implementation subsequently landed during this documentation change.</p>\n' +
    '<h2 id="what-it-does">What it does</h2>\n' +
    '<p>The core owns deeply immutable snapshots, event deduplication, cursor replay, revision ordering, unread state, drafts and command decisions. <code>initialState</code> and <code>synchronize</code> are public exports of <code>@agora/client-core</code>. A fixture adapter validates neutral wire inputs outside that package; a future React renderer will display its snapshots.</p>\n' +
    '<h2 id="why-it-exists">Why it exists</h2>\n' +
    '<p>Replacing a renderer must not replace synchronization rules. A Query cache must not become a second timeline. A native client needs equivalent replay semantics rather than borrowing assumptions embedded in DOM code.</p>\n' +
    '<h2 id="how-it-works">How it works</h2>\n' +
    '<figure class="flow"><figcaption>How it works · read in order</figcaption><ol><li><strong>Snapshot</strong><span>Read authorized state and its committed cursor together.</span></li><li><strong>Replay</strong><span>Request events strictly after that cursor; deduplicate by stream and sequence.</span></li><li><strong>Gap</strong><span>Buffer rather than invent missing events; fetch replay or a fresh snapshot.</span></li><li><strong>Projection</strong><span>Apply only newer aggregate revisions and publish immutable state.</span></li><li><strong>Renderer</strong><span>Display the projection without authorizing work or owning another timeline.</span></li></ol></figure><p>An unsupported state-changing event preserves the projection, pauses without acknowledgment and requests upgrade. Gaps buffer at most 1,000 out-of-order entries before requesting a fresh snapshot; acknowledgments cover only the applied contiguous prefix. Decimal revisions compare beyond JavaScript Number precision.</p>\n' +
    '<p>A command receipt settles a known command without advancing the timeline. Retry preserves the original ID/digest, respects denial and rate limits, and refreshes stale state. Unread counts visible message creation positions after explicit last-seen state, not edits or run-card events. Drafts stay unsent through snapshot changes; logout/revocation inputs clear private state.</p>\n' +
    '<h2 id="implementation-status">Implementation status</h2>\n' +
    '<p><strong>Built: framework-independent core.</strong> The TypeScript/Swift fixture replay proof is linked below; import/public-type guards and a no-DOM/no-Node compilation lane enforce the package boundary. Local-room L3 adds a separate <a href="local-room.html">HTTP polling adapter and minimal browser harness</a> over the same core, not transport inside this package. There is still no React room UI, production authentication or core-owned service route. U01a is milestone-qualified as of revision <code>b9c65c4</code> (see the <a href="source/evidence/U01a/outcome.json.html">milestone receipt</a>); the full R22 foundation (FG04 through FG08) remains unqualified until U01b, U01c and U01d close.</p>\n' +
